From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 12:10:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] nvme-apple: optionally wait longer for the final
 shutdown notification

At the final system shutdown a post-M4 controller gets a shutdown
notification (CC.SHN) and then CC.EN is cleared. The wait for
CSTS.SHST to report completion is ctrl->shutdown_timeout, five seconds
unless the controller reports RTD3E. If the flush takes longer, EN is
cleared on a controller that is still shutting down, and the next start
has to recover first. A loader that starts the controller with a short
ready timeout can then give up.

Add final_shn_wait_s (default 0, no change). When set, the final
shutdown waits up to that many seconds (at most 255) for the
notification to complete, and logs whether it completed and how long it
took, so a reboot test can tell whether the flush ever runs long.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/nvme/host/apple.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
index fb82b04c93..09f4fe909d 100644
--- a/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
+++ b/drivers/nvme/host/apple.c
@@ -335,6 +335,11 @@ module_param(flush_interval, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(flush_interval,
 		 "Grace period in msecs between flushes (ignored on post-M4 ANS)");
 
+static unsigned int final_shn_wait_s;
+module_param(final_shn_wait_s, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(final_shn_wait_s,
+		 "Post-M4, final system shutdown: wait up to this many seconds for the shutdown notification to complete (CSTS.SHST) before CC.EN is cleared, and log how long it took (0: the controller's own shutdown timeout, default)");
+
 static_assert(sizeof(struct nvme_command) == 64);
 static_assert(sizeof(struct apple_nvmmu_tcb) == 128);
 
@@ -1387,9 +1392,19 @@ static int apple_nvme_disable_locked(struct apple_nvme *anv, bool shutdown)
 	 * the CC.EN clear below still runs.
 	 */
 	if (READ_ONCE(anv->final_shutdown) && !apple_rtkit_is_crashed(anv->rtk)) {
+		unsigned int wait = min(READ_ONCE(final_shn_wait_s), 255U);
+		ktime_t start = ktime_get();
+
+		if (wait > anv->ctrl.shutdown_timeout)
+			anv->ctrl.shutdown_timeout = wait;
 		ret = nvme_disable_ctrl(&anv->ctrl, true);
 		if (ret)
 			dev_warn(anv->dev, "shutdown notification failed: %d\n", ret);
+		if (wait)
+			dev_info(anv->dev, "final shutdown: notification %s after %lld ms (limit %u s)\n",
+				 ret ? "NOT complete" : "complete",
+				 ktime_ms_delta(ktime_get(), start),
+				 anv->ctrl.shutdown_timeout);
 	}
 	ret = nvme_disable_ctrl(&anv->ctrl, false);
 	if (ret) {
-- 
